From 0704ffff6d867c5fc819f24633d264c15f50f283 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:54:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(render): reproduce native Bedrock classic lighting

Reconstruct the classic light-image calculation recovered locally from the
official Windows 1.26.51.1 executable with PistonDecompiler and Ghidra.
Preserve its brightness tables, weather and sunrise inputs, Nether offset,
per-channel gamma, and byte truncation in a reload-managed GPU pipeline.

Activate the same pipeline for ViaProxy clients through versioned appearance
metadata in an accepted converted server pack. Local packs and unsupported
protocol metadata cannot enable it. Resource reload and disconnect clear
the context; stale asynchronous reload completion cannot reactivate it.

Omit Java low-light vignette on supported Bedrock sessions. Native Hive
reference item surfaces have uniform texture colors, whereas 18,140 Java
white-item pixels fit the extra Java vignette within 0.33 encoded RGB bytes.
This overlay incorrectly darkened the world and held items toward edges.

Use immutable frame inputs to preserve Java refresh behavior while updating
changed native inputs. Ordinary Java sessions retain their original renderer;
End light-image inputs and enhanced native lighting remain outside this port.
